// mkit anonymous multiplayer repo — ConnectRPC wire protocol v1.
//
// A single shared mkit repository that anyone may push to anonymously, each
// write signed with an Ed25519 key (the key is the whole identity; no
// accounts, no allow-list).
//
// Storage model (framework-independent):
//   - Immutable mkit objects (commits / trees / blobs) are content-addressed
//     by their 32-byte BLAKE3 id and stored once (idempotent).
//   - Refs are the only mutable state, advanced via compare-and-swap.
//   - WatchRefs streams live ref advances for the multiplayer UI.
//
// Conventions mirror mkit-rpc/proto/mkit/rpc/v1/ssh/ssh.proto + common.proto:
//   - edition 2023.
//   - All object/ref ids are raw `bytes` = 32-byte BLAKE3 digests (never hex
//     on the wire).
//   - `RefExpectation` (the CAS enum) and `RefEntry` are shared with
//     ssh.proto via mkit/common/v1/refs.proto — one proto definition, no
//     hand-synced copies. See that file's header comment for the
//     versioning/compat contract.
//
// AUTH (transport-level, not in this proto): every unary/stream call carries
// the signed-write envelope as request metadata (headers) — `X-Public-Key`,
// `X-Signature`, `X-Digest`, `X-Created-At`, `Idempotency-Key`. The canonical
// signed string is defined in src/lib/envelope.ts and the README. Verification
// is open-write/demo-mode: any valid Ed25519 key may write any ref. Carrying
// auth in metadata (rather than proto fields) keeps the message shapes clean
// and lets the same envelope guard every procedure uniformly.
//
// ADMIN AUTH (also transport-level, separate mechanism from the write
// envelope above): PurgeRoom requires a bearer `X-Admin-Token` header equal
// to the server's `ADMIN_TOKEN` secret (see apps/repo-worker/README.md
// "Retention & backup/restore"). This is a plain shared-secret check — NOT
// an Ed25519 envelope — because a purge is an operator action with no
// room-participant author to attribute. An unset `ADMIN_TOKEN` fails
// PurgeRoom closed (`unauthenticated`) for every caller, never open.
//
// TIMESTAMP CONVENTION (mkit#795): every bare `int64` timestamp field in
// this file names its own unit — `_unix` for epoch-SECONDS, `_unix_ms` for
